<title>POLAND: KPW clears Universal new issue.</title>
<headline>KPW clears Universal new issue.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Polish Securities Commission (KPW) has cleared for public trade a new issue of up to 10 million shares of trading firm Universal SA, to be exchanged for the firm's convertible bonds the KPW said in a statement.</p>
<p>It said each bond would be exchangeable into 10,000 shares from July 1 to November 30, 2001.</p>
<p>In March Universal SA sold in a private placement 1,000 convertible bonds with a semi-annual 5.5-percent coupon.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
